# Push includes a GitHub Release

When the user says **push**, do all of this — not git only:

1. Commit pending work on `main` if needed.
2. Bump `package.json` / `package-lock.json` version (patch unless asked otherwise).
3. Push `main` to `origin`.
4. Run `npm run build:win`.
5. Publish a GitHub Release (`gh release create vX.Y.Z`) with:
   - `release/SharingStation-Setup-X.Y.Z.exe`
   - `release/SharingStation-Portable-X.Y.Z.exe`

Kiosks update from GitHub Releases, so a git push without a new release is incomplete.
